Placeholder so the Tauri bundle `resources` path exists before
`scripts/build-next.mjs` has produced the real Next.js standalone output.

Without this, `cargo check` and `tauri dev` fail on a first-time clone
with `resource path '../resources/next' doesn't exist` because the
build script hasn't populated this directory yet.

The actual standalone bundle is generated by `scripts/build-next.mjs`
and dropped here at build time. Those files are .gitignored; only this
placeholder is tracked.
